From b8d68b2eb4edf64c0e66bd2c227e251a19f80600 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:26:34 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] kcm_sddm: Gallery main page with page actions; Behavior
 sub-page as a Form that matches kcm_plasmalogin
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page types: main page Gallery, Behavior sub-page Form (docs/page-design.md). KAuth flows (save, installtheme,
uninstalltheme, sync/reset), config keys, defaults and SDDM theme.conf.user handling are unchanged.
Note KDE Linux ships Plasma Login Manager (kcm_plasmalogin), not SDDM; this page stays consistent with it.

Moved / renamed:
- Page actions at the top right in use order: Get New…, Install From File…, Behavior…, Apply Plasma Settings…
  (kcm_sddm/GetNew, InstallFromFile, Behavior, ApplyPlasmaSettings; labels unchanged).
- Empty state: Kirigami.PlaceholderMessage "No login screen themes found" with a pointer to Get New… / Install From
  File…; busy indicator only after 150 ms.
- Behavior (was Kirigami.Page + "Automatically log in: [as user:] [with session]" in one row) is now a
  KCM.SimpleKCM + Kirigami.FormLayout using the same rows and wording as kcm_plasmalogin: "Auto-login:" checkbox
  "Log in automatically", "User:", "Session:", "Log in again immediately after logging off", wallet warning as its
  own capped-width row (kcm_sddm/sddmSettings-user, User, Session, Relogin, OpenWallet). User and session are
  disabled, not hidden, while auto-login is off.
- Sections "Users" (Minimum/Maximum user UID with a one-line hint) and "Shutdown commands" ("Halt command:" /
  "Reboot command:", sentence case; file-chooser buttons get a tooltip and an accessible name).
  (kcm_sddm/MinimumUid, MaximumUid, HaltCommand, RebootCommand). Old wording is added to the layout aliases.
- Theme thumbnails load with asynchronous: true. Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_sddm.tsv (outer repo).

Speed: ThemesModel's constructor called populate(), which lists the theme folders and reads metadata.desktop,
theme.conf and theme.conf.user of every theme (src/themesmodel.cpp ctor, populate, add), before the page existed. It is
now queued with QTimer::singleShot(0); a new loaded property tells the page when the list is complete, and the current
theme (set by SddmKcm before the list existed) is re-applied after the scan. m_currentIndex was uninitialised; it is -1
now and currentTheme() no longer indexes out of range. UsersModel/SessionModel were already only created by the
Behavior sub-page. After: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-013, HIG-017, HIG-019, HIG-020, HIG-023, HIG-058.
Not built yet. Unconfirmed: nothing outside the repo's own APIs was used.

